// Signing settings that belong to whoever is building, not to the repository.
//
// Copy this to Local.xcconfig, which is not tracked, and put your own Apple Developer
// team identifier in it. Xcode reads it as the project's base configuration, so building
// from the IDE works without anyone editing — and re-committing — project.pbxproj.
//
//   cp Local.xcconfig.example Local.xcconfig
//
// Find the identifier under Xcode > Settings > Accounts, or:
//
//   xcrun security find-identity -v -p codesigning
//
// Without it the build stops at signing and says no team is set, which is the right
// failure: it names what to do rather than trying to sign as somebody else.
LOCAL_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
